        "department": null,
        "description": "Algebraic Topology is the study of topological spaces using the tools of abstract algebra. An important question in topology is whether two spaces are the same or not up to homeomorphism. It provides a way of distinguishing such spaces by defining invariants which are defined by developing algebraic structures such as groups, modules, and sequences on such spaces.\n\nThe focus of this course is to study the covering space and fundamental groups of different spaces, starting from the circle. We will see how algebra helps to distinguish two spaces. One of the main goal of this course is to prove that the fundamental group of the circle is set of integers. We will also study Seifert\u2013Van Kampen theorem, which is a tool to find the fundamental group of different topological spaces. We will also see the two Euclidean spaces are not homeomorphic unless they are of same dimension.",
        "prerequisites_mandatory": [
